From: Cencyte D <antiultra2007@gmail.com>
Subject: Delegate spatial input between threads in the private Wine runtime

Requires Wine10.20 patches0003,0004,0005,0011,0013,0014. Regenerate
requests and syscall tables. Build/mount User32, Win32u, ntdll and
wineserver together. WINE_GHUB_INPUT_DELEGATION=1 enables registration.

Observed native contract: user32 ordinals2503/2504/2505 forward to
NtUserDelegateInput/NtUserUndelegateInput/NtUserHandleDelegatedInput.
Spatial mask0x1000 targets a separate GUI thread in the same process
and desktop. A callback receives MSG/context; dispositions1/2/3 resume,
discard or defer hardware input. Explicit resolution applies to the
pending prefix, excluding an in-flight callback's message. Queued and
deferred messages are cancelled/resumed when windows or threads exit.

This opt-in x64 implementation supports the observed QS_POINTER route
only. Keyboard/mouse masks, native gesture/pointer-history behavior,
composition hit testing and general WinUI compatibility remain outside
this patch. No native Windows differential execution was performed.

